%% MSC 3 — Xn-based inter-gNB handover of a shuttle carrier mid-yard (TS 23.502 §4.9.1.2, TS 38.300 §9.2.3.2)
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant UE as Shuttle CPE
    participant S as Source gNB (MAST-A2)
    participant T as Target gNB (MAST-B2)
    participant AMF
    participant SMF
    participant UPF as Local UPF
    UE->>S: Measurement Report (A3: neighbour RSRP > serving + offset)
    S->>T: Xn Handover Request (UE context, PDU sessions, QoS flows incl. 5QI 84 GBR, PDCP SN status)
    T-->>S: Xn Handover Request Acknowledge (target cell config in RRC container)
    S->>UE: RRC Reconfiguration (handover command)
    Note over S,T: Data forwarding on Xn-U: source forwards buffered UL/DL PDCP SDUs + SN Status Transfer (next expected UL SN, DL COUNT).
    S->>T: SN Status Transfer
    S->>T: Xn-U forwarded packets
    UE->>T: Random access + RRC Reconfiguration Complete
    Note over UE,T: Interruption ≈ RRC processing + RACH + reconfig ≈ [FILL from TS 38.133 / measured]; must be < S2 PDB 30 ms budget slack. DAPS HO (TS 38.300 §9.2.3.2.1) reduces it to ~0 ms.
    T->>AMF: NGAP Path Switch Request (PDU sessions to switch, target N3 F-TEID)
    AMF->>SMF: Nsmf_PDUSession_UpdateSMContext
    SMF->>UPF: PFCP Session Modification (DL FAR → target gNB F-TEID)
    UPF-->>SMF: PFCP Session Modification Response
    UPF->>T: End marker on old tunnel (via source, forwarded)
    SMF-->>AMF: response
    AMF-->>T: NGAP Path Switch Request Acknowledge
    T->>S: Xn UE Context Release
